=== PARITY (vs web SignalCatalogPanel.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> useTelemetry/useSignalGaps + useTranslation. The web wraps
    `useSignalGaps(vehicleId)` (GET /signals/{id}/live, refetch every 5 s) + local
    search/filter/sort `useState`. The native surface mirrors the split: the P1/S8
    `SignalCatalogSource` delivers the coalesced live snapshot (the signal entries +
    isLoading + error + connection + dataUpdatedAt); the view performs NO HTTP. The
    search text / filter pill / sort mode are the view-model's own interactive state.
  Projection -> 1:1 port of the web's two `useMemo` blocks: (1) rows — staleness =
    ts ? (now - ts)/1000 : Infinity; category = !ts ? never : staleness > 300 ? stale :
    active; value ?? "—". (2) filter+sort — case-insensitive name search, the all/stale
    (stale|never)/active pill, and the staleness(desc)/alpha/category({never:0,stale:1,
    active:2}) comparators. Plus the fine `getCatalogStalenessStyle` ladder
    (Active<30 · Aging<300 · Stale>=300 · Never received) for the per-row badge, and the
    summary counts over the FULL set. Verified by executed XCTest.
  Composition -> the four `StatCard`s (Total/Active(<30s)/Stale(>5min)/Never Received),
    the glass panel with its "Refreshes every 5s" header, the `Input` search +
    filter/sort selectors (web ghost-button pills -> Apple-idiomatic segmented controls,
    same modes+labels), the `DataTable` columns (status badge/signal mono/value mono/
    lastUpdated/timeSince in level tone), the optional `selection` add/remove column
    (Plus/X + max cap), and the `dataUpdatedAt` "Last refreshed: <relative>" footer.
  Shared components -> @/components/ui -> TSGlassPanel/TSCard, TSDataTable/TSColumn (web
    DataTable), TSTextField (web Input), TSButton (web Button), a custom status chip +
    select button (mirror TSBadge/Button tokens, taking the runtime facade strings the
    LocalizedStringKey-only TSBadge can't express); @/components/data-display -> TSStatCard
    (web StatCard); @/components/feedback -> TSSkeleton (web Skeleton);
    @/components/motion -> TSFadeIn (web FadeIn). Compiled against the REAL apps/apple
    component library in the iOS+macOS typechecks below. Recharts -> none / Leaflet -> none.
  States (all render) -> loading (8 TSSkeleton rows) · empty ("No signal data available")
    · data (table; over-filtered -> inline "No signals match current filters") · error
    (retry; the P4 leaf QueryError peer — the web leaf polls and has no error chrome, so
    an upstream failure surfaces here) · stale / offline (the orthogonal `connection`
    axis -> header freshness chip + banner + one-shot auto-refresh on the stale
    transition, fitting this surface's live-polling nature, per the AcDcStatsPanel/0096
    P4 leaf contract). Each state has a #if DEBUG preview and is projection-unit-tested.
  i18n -> all 21 web source keys resolve through the P1/S10 facade with the web
    t(key,default) fallback (signalGap.status/signal/lastValue/lastUpdated/timeSince/
    totalSignals/active/stale/neverReceived/refreshInterval/filterPlaceholder/filterLabel/
    all/staleOnly/activeOnly/mostStale/az/category/noMatch/noData/lastRefreshed), plus the
    optional-selection add/remove keys (signalCatalog.addSignal/removeSignal), the 4 status
    words the web hardcodes in getCatalogStalenessStyle, and 12 native chrome/a11y keys —
    ALL present in SignalCatalogPanel.strings (39 keys). No English literals in native
    code (Text(verbatim:) over the facade).
  a11y -> the search field, both segmented controls, the refresh button, the retry button,
    the status chip, and the per-row select button each carry an accessibilityLabel; the
    select button carries .isSelected; the loading state is one labeled element;
    SignalCatalogAccessibility.rowLabel is a tested combined-value seam; Dynamic Type via
    tokens; Reduce Motion gates the TSSkeleton/TSFadeIn motion.
  Telemetry -> SignalCatalogModel.start() emits viewOpened(surface:"SignalCatalogPanel")
    (P1/S11). Asserted by a spy test (fires exactly once across repeated start()).

